Build an unofficial Windows installer from a tag

Purpose: a Windows installer of the overlay at one fixed public URL
that nobody can mistake for an official Rnote release, and that
installs beside the official Rnote instead of replacing it.

Approach: upstream's release-windows.yml also runs on the
overlay-build tag (git overlay-build), so toolchain and action updates
arrive with every rebase. Overlay steps configure the build as
'win-installer-identity=overlay' (own Inno AppId, installed as
"Rnote (overlay)") with 'version-extra=+overlay-<sha>' for the About
dialog, and upload the installer to one prerelease on that tag,
titled and described as unofficial with a link to upstream's releases.

Constraints: on a fork the release and dispatch paths of
release-windows.yml and dist.yml never run, so no general-release
installer or source archive is built there. Upstream behaviour and the
official installer are unchanged. 'just configure' interpolates
unquoted, so version-extra stays free of spaces and parentheses.
